  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Capacities for Industrial Policy - Analytics and Implementation in Mongolia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Capacities for Industrial Policy - Analytics and Implementation in Mongolia. This is a request for preparatory assistance (PA) to develop a joint project with the German Development Fund (GIZ) on improving Mongolia#s economic and investment policy. More specifically, UNIDO has been asked to contribute to a three-year project funded by the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ) and implemented by GIZ, covering three thematic areas, namely: (a) Macro-policies for sustainable industrial recovery; (b) Investment promotion; and (c) Capacity development for SMEs. The future project is going to run from 2024-2026 and has an overall budget of EUR 3 million. UNIDO#s Capacity Development and Policy Advice Unit (CDA)has been asked to contribute to one of the three thematic areas.</narrative>
  </description>
